# Agent boundaries

## Never do without an explicit user request in this turn

- `git push`, force push, `gh pr create` / merge
- `wrangler deploy`, `wrangler secret`, `neonctl`, Logto production tenant changes, `firebase deploy`, `gcloud`, production secrets changes
- Committing `.env`, credentials, service-account JSON, Patreon tokens

## Always

- Prefer fixtures + in-memory ports over live MLB/Patreon/Cloudflare/Neon/Logto
- Prove work with `pnpm verify` (and story-specific tests from `docs/v3/BACKLOG.md`)
- Update `docs/v3/BACKLOG.md` Status (`doing` → `done`) and the top Story status table in the same change set as the story
- Refuse the next story/goal while prior story work is still uncommitted (`git status` dirty for that work)
- Refuse the next story/goal while a **backlog review** is due — 3 `done` stories since the last row in the BACKLOG **Backlog reviews** table, or any drift event (`.claude/skills/backlog-review/SKILL.md`). Fresh context; `blocked` verdict stops work
- Keep domain (`packages/domain`) free of Cloudflare/Postgres/Logto/HTTP SDKs
- Follow `CLAUDE.md` conventions; if wrong, update that file — don’t rely on chat memory

## Prefer

- Smallest backlog story that advances the carried product loop
- Updating BACKLOG acceptance criteria when they prove ambiguous
- Worktree-isolated runs for unattended loops
